# TimeTrack Staging Environment Example
# Use this as a starting point for a real staging deployment.
# Copy to .env.staging (or load via your CI / deploy script) and point the Firebase values at your dedicated staging project.
# Never commit actual secrets or real project IDs that you don't want public.

# === Point these at your staging Firebase project (e.g. atd-time-tracking-staging) ===
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=...
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=atd-time-tracking-staging.firebaseapp.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=atd-time-tracking-staging
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=atd-time-tracking-staging.firebasestorage.app
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=...
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=...

# For local testing against staging (rare), you can also set:
# VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false

# When running the prod-test-user seeder against staging, you would set the non-Vite env vars instead:
# ADMIN_EMAIL=staging-admin@...
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=...
# TEST_PASSWORD=...
# (and ensure the app's Firebase config / src/firebase.js resolves to the staging project for that Node run)
